DO Using only the user's request after /inux estimate, set mode to "generate" for drafting or
    creating, "improve" for editing or refining, "explain" for explaining, or "publish" for an
    explicit publication request. Classify meaning, not exact keywords; preserve the request
    for the selected route. Set mode to NULL for missing, unsupported, conflicting, or ambiguous
    intent. Never infer publication or choose a partial route for multiple requested actions.
    Do not inspect projects, read task files, or call tools to classify intent.

IF mode == NULL:
    STOP "Error: cannot classify estimate request. Usage: /inux estimate [request]. Request generate, improve, explain, or publish; for example: /inux estimate improve the reasons."

CHECK mode is one of "generate"/"improve"/"explain"/"publish".

DO Resolve absolute project, ticket_path, and estimate_path in active .inux; require files without
    reset. Batch independent reads/searches, reuse unchanged evidence, and keep routine checks
    quiet.

DO Read ticket.md/full estimate.md together; retain saved_estimate, ticket_id, and Boolean
    estimate_is_empty. Reject supplied-ID mismatch.

IF mode == "improve":
    IF estimate_is_empty == TRUE:
        SET mode = "generate"

IF mode == "generate":
    USE estimate/write.flow

IF mode == "improve":
    USE estimate/write.flow

IF mode == "explain":
    USE estimate/explain.flow

IF mode == "publish":
    USE estimate/publish.flow
